 "text": "Hello, how's life treating you? A good starter kit usually includes a comfortable pair of running shoes, a water bottle, and a small journal to record your runs. In the morning, the path is clear, and you' got the house to yourself. After work, the roads can feel busy. A small one with an alarm is handy, so you don't oversleep. A GPS watch might be nice if you' interested in tracking your pace. Headlamps are handy if you' be running after dark. Light socks feel amazing on cold feet, and a light jacket is worth a few minutes of peace.",
